    <string name="informed_consent_header">Informed Consent</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_title">INFORMED CONSENT</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p1">We are from the team \"Mama, Aku Kecanduan HP\" from SMAN 70 Jakarta. Currently, we are conducting a research project titled \"CelfCare (Software for Indonesian Adolescent Digital Wellbeing): Control Theory-Based Screen Time Management System for Digital Health\".</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p2">This research aims to determine whether using the CelfCare app with adaptive cognitive challenge interventions can help reduce screen time duration, particularly on entertainment apps, without significantly increasing user stress levels. CelfCare is designed as digital wellbeing software that delivers short cognitive challenges in the form of mental math and pattern recognition when respondents open designated entertainment apps.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p3">The benefit of this study is providing respondents with experience using technology designed to enhance awareness of screen time usage. Additionally, the findings are expected to serve as a foundation for developing adaptive digital wellbeing software tailored to adolescents\' needs.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p4">The research methodology utilized is experimental quantitative research with a repeated measures design. Data collection is carried out through the CelfCare app and questionnaires. Respondents will use the application throughout the study period, after which screen usage data and intervention activities will be analyzed to observe changes in screen time over the measurement period.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p5">This research is conducted online via each respondent\'s smartphone. Respondents will use the CelfCare application for the designated study period. During the study, respondents are asked to use their smartphones as usual without intentionally altering their device usage habits.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p6">When respondents open designated entertainment apps selected for intervention, CelfCare will display a brief cognitive challenge before the app can be accessed. The intervention level can adjust based on the respondent\'s performance in solving challenges within pre-determined difficulty limits.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p7">Throughout the study, the app will collect necessary research data, such as total screen time, entertainment app usage duration, app launch counts, and intervention activity and performance. Respondents will also be asked to complete a questionnaire to provide feedback on their experience using the application.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p8">CelfCare is not used to read the content of messages, photos, videos, contacts, passwords, or personal conversation logs of respondents. The collected data is strictly used for research purposes.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p9">Using the application may cause mild inconvenience, such as feeling interrupted when interventions pop up or feeling discomfort when pausing entertainment app usage. Respondents might also experience difficulty when solving mental math or pattern challenges. Interventions are designed as short challenges within pre-set difficulty limits.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p10">Obtained data will be kept strictly confidential and accessible only to the research team. Research data will be stored locally on the researcher\'s laptop. Respondent identities will use codes during data processing and will not be disclosed in research reports. Research outcomes will be presented in aggregate form, tables, graphs, or statistical analyses so individual identities cannot be identified.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p11">Participation in this study is conducted according to research procedures with consent from the respondent and their parent or guardian. Respondents will receive a compensation of IDR 50,000 as appreciation for their time and participation. This compensation is not a form of coercion to join the study.</string>
    <string name="informed_consent_p12">If you have questions, trouble using the app, or feedback regarding this study, you may contact: josuaku091010@gmail.com (Joshua Leonardo Hilman Hutajulu) and daffa.satya.alif@gmail.com (Daffa Satya Alif Siregar).</string>
